</figure>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The autoregressive baselines train at <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}4</annotation></semantics></math> rather than
the zero-shot <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{\leq}20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{\leq}20</annotation></semantics></math> cap because training under longer
sequential generation exceeds our memory budget at the
global batch of <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math> (see the fine-tuning setup in
§<a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5 Fine-Tuning Setup ‣ 4 Experimental Setup ‣ DiffRetriever: Parallel Representative Tokens for Retrieval with Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
